course: dictionary
lesson: 2858
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Doll» can mean a toy, a kind person, or to dress up nicely. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Children played with balls, dolls and board games» is about toys, because children play with balls and board games. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «You're a doll» does not mean you are a toy. Someone is being praised for being kind or pretty. When you see a word you know in a new way, stop and ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Dolls» can mean toys shaped like a baby, child or person.
fact: «Doll» can also mean a pretty or kind person, as in «You're a doll.»
fact: To «doll up» means to dress up nicely for a special event. It is informal, so it is used in chatty speech.
fact: Phrases: «doll's house» is used in the UK, «dollhouse» in the US, and a «rag doll» is a doll made of cloth.
exercise: «Most Egyptians were farmers, and children played with balls, dolls and board games like senet.» What are dolls in this sentence? | Kinds of bread | *Toys shaped like children | Farm animals | Thick drinks
exercise: «You're a doll.» What does doll mean here? | *A kind, pretty person | A wooden table | A toy shaped like a baby | A dress for a party
exercise: «She dolled up for the party in a sparkly dress.» What does dolled up mean? | *Dressed up nicely for a special event | Ran a race | Lost a shoe | Fell asleep on the sofa
test: Which phrase means a toy house for dolls in the UK? | dolled up | action figure | *doll's house | rag doll
test: A «rag doll» is most likely made of what? | Stone | *Cloth | Metal | Glass
exam: Read «You're a doll, Mia, thanks for helping me.» What does doll mean, and how do you know? | Someone dressed up for a party, because Mia is thanked | *A kind person, because Mia is being thanked | A board game, because thanks is said after playing | A toy shaped like a child, because Mia likes toys
